## Import

{{ codefile "shell" "examples/resources/sapintegrationsuite_message_mapping/import.sh" }}

The ID is `<package_id>/<mapping_id>`. SAP returns no file, so if the configuration sets
`content`, the first apply uploads it, which is an in-place update and needs
`enable_unofficial`. To adopt a mapping with documented operations only, leave `content` and
`content_hash` out until you change the content.

## Limitations

- **SAP:** no documented update of the content. The provider sends a `PUT` shaped like SAP's
  documented integration flow update, which a tenant accepted in September 2026. Whether a delete removes every saved
  version or only the active one is not documented.
- **Provider:** files up to 32 MiB from local disk. Content changes made in the UI are not
  detected.

